sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Client App (Mobile / Desktop)
    participant Source as Source Server (Local / Self-Hosted / Cloud)
    participant Outbox as Sync Outbox (UUID v7 ordered)
    participant Dispatcher as Webhook Dispatcher (Sync Worker)
    participant Dest as Destination Server
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Queue

    Note over Client,Source: Local change → outbox write
    Client->>Source: POST /resource (e.g. new appointment)
    Source->>Source: persist domain change
    Source->>Outbox: append event (uuid v7, category, payload)
    Source-->>Client: 200 OK

    Note over Dispatcher,Dest: Server-to-server federation (chunked snapshots by data category)
    loop Every poll interval
        Dispatcher->>Outbox: read pending events
        Note right of Dispatcher: split into chunks by category — entities, doctors, patients, records, inventory, billing, …
        Dispatcher->>Dest: POST /sync/inbound (chunk N), HMAC-SHA256 signed
        alt 200 OK
            Dest->>Dest: apply chunk, then persist watermark per category
            Dest-->>Dispatcher: ack { last_uuid }
            Dispatcher->>Outbox: mark events delivered
        else 4xx (validation)
            Dest-->>Dispatcher: 4xx error detail
            Dispatcher->>DLQ: park chunk + reason
        else 5xx / timeout
            Note right of Dispatcher: exponential backoff, up to 5 retries / 24h
            Dispatcher->>Dest: retry POST /sync/inbound
            alt all retries fail
                Dispatcher->>DLQ: park chunk
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Client,Source: Mobile pull (watermark)
    Client->>Source: GET /sync/pull?since={watermark}&limit=N
    Source-->>Client: { events, next_watermark }
    Client->>Client: apply, advance watermark

    Note over Client,Source: Offline queue (mobile makes changes while disconnected)
    Client->>Client: append to local SQLite outbox
    Client->>Client: stay offline…
    Client->>Source: POST /sync/push (queued events) on reconnect
    Note right of Source: conflict resolution — clinical = server-authoritative, non-clinical = admin-configured
    Source->>Source: validate, conflict-resolve
    Source-->>Client: { applied, conflicted, rejected }
